Switch the site from black/violet to the teal palette

User selected option 4 from the palette comparison and asked to drop purple
as the accent entirely.

Token work:
- Replace the :root block with the teal set: base #0a1214 lifted well off
  #000 so cards read as surfaces rather than holes, accent #2dd4bf.
- Rename --accent-purple{,-light,-dark} to --accent{,-light,-dark}. The old
  names described a colour the site no longer used, and would have misled the
  next edit.
- Rename --shadow-purple to --shadow-accent for the same reason.

The bulk of the work was 113 hardcoded rgba(139, 92, 246, …) values across
seven stylesheets that the token rename could not reach. Converted each hue
triple (accent, accent-light, accent-dark) in both legacy and modern
space-separated syntax. Verified zero purple remains in source or built CSS.

Follow-on fixes the palette exposed:
- Navbar scrim and mobile menu used rgba(0,0,0,…) tuned for a #000 page; on
  the new base that reads as grey haze over the content. Tinted toward the
  page base instead.
- Projects modal overlay, same issue.
- Contact availability dot was #4ADE80 green — too close to teal to read as
  a distinct status signal. Now uses the accent with a soft pulse ring, and
  the panel gradient runs darker rather than lighter so it stays visible
  against the lighter teal base.
- GitHub channel card in Contact used a violet accent. GitHub's mark is
  monochrome, so it now uses GitHub's light foreground grey.

Tech logo contrast:
- Audited all 23 brand tints against the logo tile background (the actual
  surface they sit on, not the page). Pandas #150458, YOLOv8 #111111 and
  C++ #00599C were at 1.2–2.1:1 and genuinely invisible on the new base.
- Lifted each to a lighter tint of the same hue, preserving brand identity
  since the name sits beside the mark. All 23 now clear 3:1.
- Obsidian and the generic SQL tint were near-violet and clashed; SQL moved
  to a desaturated teal. Obsidian keeps a violet because that is its actual
  brand colour and the stack is intentionally brand-coloured.

Also updated theme-color in index.html and manifest.json to the new base, and
removed the now-obsolete palette-preview.html.

Verified: npm run build compiles clean with no warnings; all five routes
serve 200 from the production build; built CSS contains #2dd4bf 59 times and
zero occurrences of the old violet.